#Service staff specialisation added by the code mod (DLLMods/Cybersecurity)
Cybersecurity "Cybersecurity"

#Lawsuit subjects raised when a cyber incident is not contained in time (DLLMods/Cybersecurity)
CyberBreach "Failing to protect customer data from a breach"
CyberDDoS "Failing to keep services online during a DDoS attack"
CyberPhishing "Failing to protect customers from a phishing campaign"
CyberRansomware "Failing to contain a ransomware attack"

#Lawsuit subjects (shown as the reason for the lawsuit)
BackupMining "Mining customer backups for profit"
BadUpdate "Bricking customers with a bad update"
BrowsingDataSale "Selling customer browsing history"
ComplianceTheater "Faking compliance results"
DefaultCredentials "Shipping default admin credentials"
EscrowedVaultKeys "Secretly keeping copies of customers' vault keys"
ExploitStockpile "Hoarding and selling vulnerabilities"
ExposedDebugPort "Shipping devices with an open debug port"
MaliciousBusiness "Malicious business practices"
MisissuedCertificates "Issuing certificates without validation"
PrivacyViolation "Privacy violation"
SampleResale "Reselling customer malware samples"
TelemetryResale "Reselling customer telemetry"
UnauthorizedModification "Unauthorized modification of user settings"
UnauthorizedSurveillance "Unauthorized surveillance"
WeakKeys "Shipping predictable cryptographic keys"

#Notifications ({0} is the product name)
BackdoorNotification "Security researchers found the government backdoor in {0}, which will hurt your market recognition"
BackupMiningNotification "Customers discovered that {0} was mining their backups and selling what it found"
